\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b How the commands fit together\b0{\*\bkmkstart how-the-commands-fit-together}{\*\bkmkend how-the-commands-fit-together}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 The module has a lot of commands because each one has a single, well-defined job. Mixing them into one "do everything" command would make it impossible to test individual steps or re-run just the part that failed.\par
