lbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \b Lookup\b0\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 Get-OneViewServerList\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Lists all servers managed by OneView. Reuses the active session.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \b Lookup\b0\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 Get-OneViewServerTarget\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Resolves a single server by name, serial, iLO IP, or bay. Reuses the active session.\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \b Review\b0\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 Configure-PhysicalBuild\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Read-only 4-eye review. Shows the full deployment plan, including all destructive actions, and waits for you to type {\f1 APPROVE\f0}. Automatically places server in OneView maintenance mode before build (use {\f1 -NoMaintenanceMode\f0} to skip).\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \b Monitor\b0\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 Start-InstallMonitor\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Watches an in-progress installation and reports progress.\cell}\row
\pard\sa80\fs22 \b Which command should I use?\b0\par
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab "Is OneView up?" -> {\f1 Test-ServerConnectivity\f0}\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab "I need to run several OneView commands" -> {\f1 Connect-OneView\f0} once, then use {\f1 Get-OneViewServerList\f0} / {\f1 Get-OneViewServerTarget\f0} freely\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab "Show me what the deploy would do" -> {\f1 Configure-PhysicalBuild\f0}\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab "Actually deploy to the server" -> {\f1 Configure-PhysicalBuild -Deploy\f0} (or {\f1 -Execute\f0}) after review\par
\pard\li360\ri360\sa80\fs22\i \b Single public build command:\b0 {\f1 Configure-PhysicalBuild\f0} is the only build command you run from the terminal. When you type {\f1 APPROVE\f0} (or pass {\f1 -Deploy\f0}), it internally executes the build pipeline - OneView resolution, maintenance mode enable, iLO mount, OS install, post-build validation, and maintenance mode disable. \i0\par
\pard\li360\ri360\sa80\fs22\i ### Safe vs destructive commands (read this first)\par\nOn a live, regulated banking appliance you must never lose a client server, its data, or impact a workload. Run the \b non-destructive\b0 commands first to identify and validate the exact target and media; the \b destructive\b0 ones are gated by a mandatory {\f1 -GuardRail\f0} regex (the \i resolved\i0 server name must match) and prompt for confirmation.\par\n\par\n| Safety | Commands | Effect |\par\n|--------|----------|--------|\par\n| \b Non-destructive / safe\b0 | {\f1 Test-ServerConnectivity\f0}, {\f1 Get-OneViewConnectionStatus\f0}, {\f1 Get-OneViewServerList\f0}, {\f1 Get-OneViewServerTarget\f0}, {\f1 Test-BuildParams\f0}, {\f1 Test-PreBuildValidation\f0}, {\f1 Start-InstallMonitor\f0}, {\f1 Invoke-IloRedfish -Action Status\\|Eject\f0}, {\f1 Invoke-OpsRampClient\f0}, {\f1 Disconnect-OneView\f0} | Read-only lookups, path/validation checks, or status monitoring. No reboot, mount, or change to any server. Safe on the live appliance. |\par\n| \b Destructive\b0 | {\f1 Configure-PhysicalBuild\f0} (APPROVE confirmation gate) | {\f1 Configure-PhysicalBuild\f0} reviews the plan and, on typing {\f1 APPROVE\f0} or passing {\f1 -Deploy\f0}/{\f1 -Execute\f0}, \b executes the destructive build\b0 internally - OneView resolution, maintenance mode enable, ISO mount + reboot (wipe/reinstall), post-build validation, and maintenance mode disable. Gated by {\f1 -GuardRail\f0}; {\f1 -DryRun\f0} prints the plan without acting. \b Automatically places the server into OneView maintenance mode before destructive operations\b0 (use {\f1 -NoMaintenanceMode\f0} to skip). |\par\n\par\n\b Recommended pre-flight review (no change is made until you type {\f1 APPROVE\f0} on {\f1 Configure-PhysicalBuild\f0}, or pass {\f1 -Deploy\f0}/{\f1 -Execute\f0}):\b0 {\f1 Get-OneViewServerTarget\f0} -> {\f1 Test-BuildParams\f0} (ISO path) -> {\f1 Test-PreBuildValidation\f0} -> {\f1 Configure-PhysicalBuild -GuardRail '<server>'\f0} (review, then type {\f1 APPROVE\f0} or pass {\f1 -Deploy\f0} to authorize the real run).\i0\par
\pard\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw20\brsp20\sa120\sb120\par
