\pard\li360\ri360\sa80\fs22\i \b Short aliases:\b0 the long (canonical) parameter names are {\f1 -OneViewHost\f0}, {\f1 -ServerIdentifier\f0}, {\f1 -IdentifierType\f0}, etc.; every one also has a short alias (e.g. {\f1 -OVHost\f0}, {\f1 -SrvrId\f0}, {\f1 -IdTyp\f0}). The long and short forms are interchangeable - the router, {\f1 request_types.json\f0}, and existing automation continue to use the long names.\i0\par
\pard\li360\ri360\sa80\fs22\i \b One-parameter targeting:\b0 {\f1 -IdentifierType\f0} defaults to {\f1 Auto\f0}, which tries Name, Serial, OneViewName, iLO IP, then EnclosureBay in turn. So {\f1 -ServerIdentifier <value>\f0} (or its alias {\f1 -SrvrId <value>\f0}) alone resolves the server - you do \b not\b0 need to pass {\f1 -IdentifierType\f0}. The explicit type is only required to disambiguate when a value could match more than one form.\i0\par
\pard\li360\ri360\sa80\fs22\i \b Note:\b0 the short alias is {\f1 -SrvrId\f0} (with the \b {\f1 r\f0}\b0). {\f1 -SrvId\f0} (without the {\f1 r\f0}) is NOT a valid parameter.\i0\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 If {\f1 -OneViewHost\f0} is omitted, the command checks {\f1 $global:ConnectedSessions\f0} for an active HPEOneView module session.\par
