\pard\sa120\sb120\fs28\b ISO Image Naming & SMB Shares\b0{\*\bkmkstart iso-image-naming-smb-shares}{\*\bkmkend iso-image-naming-smb-shares}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 How ISO filenames are generated and how local ISO paths are exposed to the iLO BMC over SMB/CIFS. Read this before passing a local path to a deploy command so you know the expected filename and the share name the iLO will mount.\par
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b Bootable ISO filename convention\b0{\*\bkmkstart bootable-iso-filename-convention}{\*\bkmkend bootable-iso-filename-convention}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 When building a ConfigMgr bootable ISO, use the standard naming convention:\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2\cf2{\f1 WinSrv2025_HPE_BootableMedia_v<Major.Minor>.iso\f0}\par}
\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab {\f1 <Major>\f0} / {\f1 <Minor>\f0} come from {\f1 -VersionMajor\f0} (default {\f1 1\f0}) and {\f1 -VersionMinor\f0} (default {\f1 0\f0}).\par\pard\li360\fi-360\fs22\'95\tab If a file already exists at the resolved path it is reused; pass explicit {\f1 -VersionMajor\f0}/{\f1 -VersionMinor\f0} or a unique {\f1 -OutputPath\f0} to control the name.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 Example generated names:\par
\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Scenario\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Resulting file\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Default build\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 WinSrv2025_HPE_BootableMedia_v1.0.iso\f0}\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx4513\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9026{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Custom version\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 WinSrv2025_HPE_BootableMedia_v2.1.iso\f0}\cell}\row
\pard\sa120\sb120\fs24\b ISO path requirements (no local drives)\b0{\*\bkmkstart iso-path-requirements-no-local-drives}{\*\bkmkend iso-path-requirements-no-local-drives}\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 The iLO BMC is a separate physical controller and \b cannot\b0 read local drives ({\f1 C:\\\f0}, {\f1 H:\\\f0} on a local disk) on your workstation. Always supply a \b network-accessible path to the file\b0 - this module \b does not\b0 auto-create SMB shares and \b never\b0 requires Administrator privileges (regulated banking environment).\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 All of the following work and resolve to the address iLO mounts as virtual media (SMB/UNC paths are converted to a {\f1 cifs://...\f0} URL; HTTPS/NFS URLs are used directly):\par
\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Format\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Example\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Notes\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 HTTPS URL\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 https://artifacts.internal.example.com/isos/win2025.iso\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Used directly; iLO downloads - no auth prompt\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 NFS path\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 nfs://fileserver/export/win2025.iso\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Used directly; iLO mounts via NFS\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 UNC/SMB path (backslash)\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 \\\\fileserver\\isos\\win2025.iso\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Converted to {\f1 cifs://...\f0}; ensure iLO can reach the share\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 UNC/SMB path (forward slash)\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 //fileserver/isos/win2025.iso\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Same as above - Windows treats {\f1 //\f0} and {\f1 \\\\\f0} as identical\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 CIFS/SMB URL\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 cifs://fileserver/isos/win2025.iso\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Used directly (round-trips the URL this tool emits)\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 SMB URL alias\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 smb://fileserver/isos/win2025.iso\f0}\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Normalised to {\f1 cifs://...\f0}\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Mapped network drive\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 {\f1 H:\\win2025.iso\f0} (H: maps to {\f1 \\\\fileserver\\isos\f0})\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Expanded to its UNC share, then {\f1 cifs://...\f0}\cell}\row
\pard\li360\ri360\sa80\fs22\i \b Point at the file, not the share.\b0 Supply the full path to the {\f1 .iso\f0} (or firmware {\f1 .zip\f0}/folder), e.g. {\f1 \\\\fileserver\\isos\\win2025.iso\f0}. A bare {\f1 \\\\fileserver\\isos\\\f0} with no filename is not a deployable image.\i0\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 \b Not supported:\b0 local drives ({\f1 C:\\isos\\...\f0}, or a letter mapped to a \i local\i0 disk). Passing one fails with an error telling you to supply an SMB/UNC or HTTPS path instead.\par
\pard\li360\ri360\sa80\fs22\i \b Full format reference:\b0 see Path Parameter Formats for every accepted {\f1 -ExternalIsoPath\f0} / {\f1 -IsoPath\f0} / {\f1 -FirmwareFolders\f0} format, including the single-slash {\f1 /server/share\f0} autocorrection and the list of unsupported local paths.\i0\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2\cf2{\f1 # Any of these work - pick the form that matches how your file is shared:Configure-PhysicalBuild -ServerIdentifier srv01 -ExternalIsoPath '\\\\fileserver\\isos\\win2025.iso' -GuardRail 'srv01' # UNC (backslash)Configure-PhysicalBuild -ServerIdentifier srv01 -ExternalIsoPath '//fileserver/isos/win2025.iso' -GuardRail 'srv01' # UNC (forward slash)Configure-PhysicalBuild -ServerIdentifier srv01 -ExternalIsoPath 'cifs://fileserver/isos/win2025.iso' -GuardRail 'srv01' # CIFS URLConfigure-PhysicalBuild -ServerIdentifier srv01 -ExternalIsoPath 'H:\\win2025.iso' -GuardRail 'srv01' # Mapped driveConfigure-PhysicalBuild -ServerIdentifier srv01 -ExternalIsoPath 'https://artifacts.internal.example.com/isos/win2025.iso' -GuardRail 'srv01'\f0}\par}
